# Cloudflare Pages reads this file and adds these response headers to every
# request it matches, no Function needed - see
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS) tells browsers "always use HTTPS for this
# site, never even try plain http://" for the next `max-age` seconds. Pages
# already forces HTTPS on its own, but without this header a browser has no
# way to know that ahead of time - the very first request from someone who
# types "valostep.win" with no "https://" (or clicks an old http:// link)
# still goes out over plain HTTP for one round trip before Cloudflare
# redirects it, which is the exact gap HSTS closes, and it's what Cloudflare's
# own security scanner flags as "Domains without HSTS".
#
# max-age=63072000 is 2 years (Cloudflare/browser-recommended value).
# includeSubDomains is left off on purpose - it would also apply this policy
# to every subdomain of valostep.win (e.g. a future mail. or status.
# subdomain), and that's only safe to turn on once you're sure every
# subdomain you'll ever use is HTTPS-only. Same reasoning for leaving off
# `preload`: it gets this domain baked into browsers' built-in HSTS list,
# which is great for security but painful to undo (removal can take months
# to reach everyone), so it's worth adding only once you're fully confident
# in the HTTPS setup. Both are one-line additions here later if you want them.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000
